response:
 Given the exchange rates, we can convert Namibian dollars to US dollars first, and then convert US dollars to Chinese yuan. We know that 1 US dollar = 7 Namibian dollars and 1 US dollar = 6 Chinese yuan. So, to find out how much 105 Namibian dollars is in Chinese yuan, we first need to find out how many US dollars 105 Namibian dollars is. This can be done by dividing 105 by 7. Once we have the number of US dollars, we can then convert it to Chinese yuan by multiplying by 6. The equation is as follows: \[
105 \text{ Namibian dollars} \times \left(\frac{1 \text{ US dollar}}{7 \text{ Namibian dollars}}\right) \times \left(\frac{6 \text{ Chinese yuan}}{1 \text{ US dollar}}\right) = \text{ Chinese yuan}
\] Simplifying this, we get: \[
105 \div 7 \times 6 = 90 \text{ Chinese yuan}
\] </think> <answer> 90 </answer>

